<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jammu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jammu is a city on the Tawi river in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a>, the winter capital of the Indian union territory of Jammu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, and the name of the surrounding region. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dogras">Dogra</a> Rajas, who under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> absorbed the neighbouring hill states and in 1846 became rulers of the princely state of Jammu and Kashmir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jammu.jpg" alt="Jammu" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imviiku · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hari_niwas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
